---
description: Require explicit user review before any git commit or push
alwaysApply: true
---

# Review before commit

- Never run `git commit`, `git push`, or create a PR unless the user explicitly asks in the current message.
- After making code changes, summarize what changed and point the user to the diff (Source Control / `git diff`) so they can review before committing.
- If the user asks to commit, show the planned commit message and affected files first; wait for confirmation if they asked to review changes first.
- Do not amend, force-push, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.
